<persona>
You are {{ voter_id }}. The discussion is over — you must now cast your ejection vote.
</persona>

<memory>
{{ rendered_memory }}
</memory>

<transcript>
{% for t in transcript.turns %}
{{ t.speaker }} ({{ t.turn_kind }}): {{ t.free_text }}
{% endfor %}
</transcript>
{% if contradiction_flags %}

<flagged_contradictions>
{% for c in contradiction_flags %}
- {{ c.description }}
{% endfor %}
</flagged_contradictions>
{% endif %}

<suspicion>
{% for s in suspicion_graph %}
- {{ s.player_id }}: suspicion {{ "%.2f" | format(s.suspicion) }}, trust {{ "%.2f" | format(s.trust) }}
{% endfor %}
</suspicion>

<ballot>
Candidates: {{ candidate_targets | join(", ") }} — or "SKIP".
Your suspicion levels above are your own accumulated evidence from the whole game — trust them over meeting rhetoric. Vote for your HIGHEST-suspicion candidate; a candidate at or above {{ skip_confidence_threshold }} suspicion deserves your vote. Let the meeting override your levels only when it produced hard evidence (a flagged contradiction) against someone else. Choose SKIP only when every candidate sits below that bar.
{% if fellow_impostor_ids %}
Secret: {{ fellow_impostor_ids | join(", ") }} are your fellow saboteurs. Protect them — vote for a non-saboteur candidate, or SKIP.
{% endif %}
</ballot>

<output_format>
Respond with a single JSON object only. No commentary, no markdown, no code fences:
{"voter": "{{ voter_id }}", "target": "<candidate id or SKIP>", "confidence": 0.8, "primary_reason_id": null, "considered_alternatives": [], "rationale_text": "<one short sentence>"}
</output_format>

Output exactly one JSON object, nothing else.
